    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but some people say the \"financial returns\" are mostly just correlation, not causation. like, is it the DEI stuff that's helping, or are just successful companies more likely to have these programs because they can afford them? do you have any data that actually shows a direct causal link, or is it all just a bit vague?",
