      "content": "While establishing strict causal links is challenging, rigorous longitudinal studies using propensity score matching have found that companies with effective DEI programs outperform their non-DEI peers by up to 36% in profit margin. Researchers control for potential confounding variables like company size and industry, suggesting the programs themselves drive success rather than simply reflecting a higher budget. However, the data often shows that \"inclusive\" approaches differ from generic training; only those that actively integrate DEI into core business strategy demonstrate a clear positive causal impact on profitability.",
