      "content": "that 36% number sounds pretty massive though. if the data is that clear, then why is there even a debate? it feels like most of the pushback comes from people who just don't want to deal with the changes, rather than actual evidence that it doesn't work. is there any legitimate evidence against it, or is the skepticism just being used to stall progress?",
